1. Licensor and scope

The Licensor is Per Anders Molberg. "Covered Material" means the original code,
documentation, tests, notebooks, project configuration and other original project
material that the Licensor makes available under these terms, including original
material developed with assistants or language models to the extent the Licensor
owns or can license the applicable rights. These terms do not assert ownership
of material or rights that the Licensor does not own or control.

The following are excluded from Covered Material:
(a) learned model artifacts covered by LICENSE-WEIGHTS, as defined below;
(b) third-party code, content, dependencies, datasets and assets, including
    upstream portions of vendored components, which retain their own terms;
(c) material explicitly supplied under another license or agreement.

A filename, directory location, or binary format alone does not determine which
license applies. See NOTICE and docs/LICENSING.md for component boundaries.

2. Free noncommercial permission

Subject to these terms, the Licensor grants everyone a worldwide, nonexclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to use, inspect, run, copy, modify and redistribute
Covered Material, including modified versions, solely for noncommercial purposes.
This includes personal study, hobby use, and genuinely noncommercial research,
education and community projects. Ordinary noncommercial use is available
worldwide. AI Training Use is subject to the additional conditions in section 9,
which prevail over this permission. Noncommercial redistribution must be free of
charge, preserve this license and applicable copyright and attribution notices,
and identify modifications without implying endorsement by the Licensor.

Recipients receive permission directly from the Licensor under these terms.
You may not grant broader rights to the Licensor's Covered Material, remove its
restrictions, or present it as available under a permissive commercial license.
Modifications and inclusion in another project do not remove these conditions
from the Covered Material contained in that modified or combined work.

3. Commercial use requires a separate agreement

Without a separate written commercial license agreement with the Licensor,
you may not use Covered Material for commercial purposes, sell or resell it,
or charge money for access to it or for a product or service that uses it.

"Commercial purposes" includes use directed toward commercial advantage,
revenue or business operations, including internal business use; commercial
research or development; incorporation into paid products or services; paid
hosting, subscriptions, consulting or support using Covered Material; resale;
and monetization through advertising or other required consideration. Charging
only to recover costs does not create an exception. An organization's legal
form, tax status or educational purpose does not by itself make a use
noncommercial. Voluntary donations that are not required for access or services
and do not support a commercial use do not alone make a use commercial.

Commercial permission must come from the Licensor, not merely from a distributor
or contributor who lacks authority to grant it. The agreement may be free of
charge; these terms impose no minimum fee or royalty. Requests may be directed
to Per Anders Molberg through the project's GitHub account, Nysgjerrigper.

4. Learned-model exception

Learned model parameters, trained weights, fitted numerical coefficients,
learned trees and other learned model state that the Licensor releases as
trained artifacts are available under the MIT license in LICENSE-WEIGHTS,
including for commercial use. This includes non-executable metadata necessary
to load and interpret those learned artifacts. Using those artifacts independently does not require a commercial agreement
with the Licensor. This permission does not extend to Covered Material bundled
with an artifact: architecture or runtime source, custom executable classes,
training/inference scripts, feature engineering, optimization code, or project
configuration remain subject to their own licenses. Serialization does not
convert embedded executable project code into unrestricted model weights.

Training hyperparameters, tuning-study configuration and trial histories are
project configuration, not learned weights. Third-party models or data cannot
be relicensed by this exception. Artifact recipients must retain the applicable
MIT notice and any separate third-party notices.

