9. Additional conditions for AI Training Use

"AI Training Use" means reproducing, extracting, collecting, transforming or
otherwise using Covered Material or its protected expression as training data,
training targets, examples or feedback to develop or improve a machine-learning
model. It includes pretraining, fine-tuning, continued training, reinforcement
learning, distillation, and synthetic-data generation for those purposes,
including through intermediate datasets, translations, paraphrases or other
transformations that retain protected expression. Preparing or supplying such
material for another person's AI Training Use is subject to the same conditions.
Facts, ideas and independently created material remain outside this definition.

Merely running or modifying the project's forecasting, training or optimization
software for an otherwise permitted purpose is not AI Training Use of its source
or documentation. Ordinary inference, retrieval and assistant-assisted development
are not AI Training Use unless Covered Material is also used to train or improve
a model. Other license conditions, including noncommercial use, still apply.

AI Training Use is permitted only if BOTH of the following conditions hold:
(a) Every model trained or improved with Covered Material is an Open Model.
(b) Every company or other organization conducting, directing or commissioning
    that use, or for whose specific benefit it is conducted, is a Qualifying
    European Entity. Individuals acting independently for personal purposes
    remain subject to (a); acting for an organization does not avoid (b).
These conditions apply equally to commercial and noncommercial organizations,
research partnerships, affiliates, contractors and intermediaries. Section 3
continues to require a separate agreement for any commercial use.

An "Open Model" is a model whose complete trained parameters (including weights,
adapters and other learned state), architecture, inference and training source
code, training configuration, and sufficiently detailed information about the
training data and process to enable a skilled person to reproduce and modify
its training are publicly available without charge. Those releases must permit
anyone to use, study, modify and redistribute the model and released code for
any purpose, including commercially, without individual approval or a separate
commercial agreement. API-only access, a research-only release, or public weights
alone do not qualify. The required releases must occur no later than the first
use of the resulting model beyond training, validation and evaluation necessary
to prepare that release, and remain available for as long as the model is used
or distributed. A plan to release later does not authorize closed deployment.

"European Territory" means the European Economic Area (the European Union,
Norway, Iceland and Liechtenstein), the United Kingdom, and Switzerland.

A "Qualifying European Entity" is an entity incorporated or legally established
in the European Territory whose actual headquarters, central administration and
principal place of management are located there. Every ultimate controlling
entity must meet the same requirements, and every natural person exercising
ultimate control must be habitually resident in the European Territory. Where
there is no controlling owner, the entity's actual governing body and management
must exercise ultimate decision-making authority from the European Territory.

"Control" means the direct or indirect ability, individually or jointly, to
direct management or material policies, through ownership, voting rights, board
appointment rights, contractual arrangements, decisive veto rights, trusts,
nominees or otherwise. It includes effective control without majority ownership
and is assessed through every intermediate entity. A passive minority investment
alone does not establish control. European incorporation, a registered office,
tax residence, local computing infrastructure or an intermediate European holding
company does not alone establish qualification.

AI Training Use by, on behalf of, at the direction of, or for the specific benefit
of a non-qualifying organization is prohibited, including through a European
subsidiary, affiliate, contractor, research institution, proxy or arrangement
intended to circumvent these conditions. Qualification must be maintained during
AI Training Use; outsourcing or transferring that use does not remove the gates.
Distributors must preserve these terms with Covered Material supplied for AI
Training Use and may not grant permission to bypass them.

To the extent applicable law permits reservation, the Licensor expressly reserves
text-and-data-mining rights for AI Training Use outside these conditions,
including under Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790. This reservation does
not restrict mandatory statutory exceptions or claim control of third-party
rights. Section 9 does not alter LICENSE-WEIGHTS, prior grants applicable to
